desc:TwoStorms Delay
//tags: delay echo
//author: TwoStorms
//version: 2.0
//
// A two-line delay with an Act built in: its output gain, meters, Auto (Target, Match, Reference),
// Drive link and Finale are a TwoStorms Act, so TwoStorms Gain Stage lists and stages it like one.
// Two independent delay lines (A and B), each with its own left and right time (free or tempo-synced), feedback,
// ping-pong or stereo, up to four taps, level, pan and width. The lines run in parallel, in series (A to B or B to A) or linked.
// In every line's loop: low cut, high cut and a bell, diffusion, pitch shift or reverse, saturation (24 styles),
// and a character: clean, tape (wow, flutter, loss), BBD or lo-fi, with an age control.
// Ducking (from the input or the sidechain), freeze, eight modulation slots (LFO, envelope follower, MIDI),
// A shared reverb (with optional shimmer) after the lines, reverse that follows the beat, and a High quality mode
// (6-point interpolation, aligned pitch shifting, 2x oversampled saturation).
// A/B sets with level-matched Bypass and Swap.
// Needs REAPER 6.74 or newer.
slider1:0<0,3,1{2,4,6,8}>-Channels
slider2:0<0,2,1{Auto,Always,Never}>-Finale (Auto = the last Act in the chain)
slider3:0<0,2,1{Peak,RMS,LUFS}>-Auto measure
